           <item>
            <widget class="QLabel" name="label">
             <property name="text">
              <string>&lt;h1&gt;Visual ICC&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
This is a tool for generating ICC files using visual methods, like comparing differently patterned/colored swatches. &lt;b&gt;This is not a calibration tool and does not replace using a hardware measuring device if a true calibration is needed.&lt;/b&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
This works to create a useable gamma setting (and pleasing white-balance at some time in the future), though.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
As a quick check, the images below should appear uniform in color. If they appear to have pairs of diagonally different brightness blocks, at least some improvement can be done. This assumes this specific window is using your prefered icc profile for this display. This usually can be set in the Display settings, but could also be overriden per application/window. Display brightness setting can also play a role.
&lt;/p&gt;</string>
             </property>
             <property name="alignment">
              <set>Qt::AlignmentFlag::AlignLeading|Qt::AlignmentFlag::AlignLeft|Qt::AlignmentFlag::AlignTop</set>
             </property>
             <property name="wordWrap">
              <bool>true</bool>
             </property>
             <property name="margin">
              <number>6</number>
             </property>
            </widget>
           </item>
